- JS lane cannot execute locally (no node_modules); validate the { timeout: 20000 } option shape against vitest 4.1.10 docs/precedent in-repo, and note that full JS validation happens when PR #2 CI reruns after this fix merges;
- check PR #4's own CI (run 34739789508 on 9216fcae): the non-queued lanes that DID execute (ruff blocking, e2e, macOS, supply-chain, osv, case-collision, history) must be success; attribution failure and Python/Windows/JS queues are structural pre-adapter base-workflow issues (documented in t_60055c4e comment 3528), NOT defects of this commit — verify they match that explanation;
- record PASS/BLOCK with reproducible commands, exit codes and URLs;
- do NOT merge anything, do NOT apply ci-reviewed label, do NOT touch frozen heads fa343068 / 5a46bf1d, do not deploy or update installed Hermes.

Rollback if blocked: revert of single commit 9216fcaef250565fecabe865eacc2ba8b62b75c4 (parent a35724c1e75730cb34758c35bf14a86485a8d702).

