# Context: what the controller is and why it waits

PR12 (`6981b7e97f64d736f420b8332397f2976f2d2b8b`, draft) contains a v3 reducer/next-bet controller. It must NOT merge until: (a) the release attestation gate exists (t_fdeb5580 chain), (b) the exact-head self-verification lane exists — PR15 `e031b47c7936f0edb74f20c9778f2deaaa717778` (this prerequisite is now being QA'd), (c) metric collector PR14 merges first and produces weekly snapshots.

Your task: rebase the PR12 controller work onto the post-attestation codex/company-os, resolve the 1.2.7 version conflict, renumber to the next free patch (e.g. 1.2.9, bump all 4 pins + CHANGELOG "reserved by controller lane" note), re-run full suite twice (normal + HERMES_KANBAN_TASK=t_ci_simulated), push, keep PR in draft, comment exact new head + test counts on your card.

Hard rules (owner approved the ordered plan; merge/deploy only via the attested ops chain):
- no merge, no deploy, no cron registration, no live controller runs — shadow only after the full attested chain;
- exact-head QA via the new read-only verifier lane (PR15 lane) — open QA children with the verifier recipe (gh pr view/checks + gh api GET + sha256 via local files only);
- version 1.2.7 is now taken by PR15 — do not reuse;
- controller shadow soak may start only after its exact-head QA passes and PR14 is merged (dependency).

## Acceptance
- PR12 rebased, CI green on new head, exact head SHA reported;
- controller.py compiles; no policy classifier changes; no live registration;
- PR marked ready for review but NOT merged;
- card result carries: PR link, head SHA, test evidence, explicit "awaiting PR14 merge + attested chain" status line.

Kill criteria: any policy classification deny loop (>2 same failures) → block card with `same_failure_loop` note, stop work.
